// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Batty 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P157122556" "Notes on the ritual"
// DetailString :
"P4210813231" "These notes are all about the Legacy Chain's ritual. <br><br>'The first group is reporting results. Now that we know what to look for, it did not take long to verify it. So obvious, why didn't we see it before? It explains so much. <br>The second group has begun. They're trying to trace it out now. It's an immense power, spreading out everywhere. Does Dr. Aeon even know? He must suspect! It would explain the clockwork, too. The ones out here, they're not under the control of the Clockwork King of Paragon City. They're under it's control. Incredible. <br><br>First group is back in. They've traced it's origin back. We will need Henri's journals. We must get them, and soon. <br>The second group had to stop. They've been discovered. The Circle is watching. They're planning something. Something only their twisted minds could comprehend. I worry even more about Tarikoss. I warned the others that he would go to far and should have been stopped earlier. It may be too late know. I only hope I can get what we've discovered to my superiors.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Powerdown 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3906120573" "The Foreman's story"
// DetailString :
"P1769865006" "The PTS forman told you a bit about what happened right before the attack: <br><br>'We didn't have any warning. The PTS had a sudden power drop, like the Volcano went dead. Then the attack hit us before we could even figure out what went wrong.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Diversion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P958325396" "The cacklings of Zurabsal"
// DetailString :
"P2670476698" "Right before his defeat, Zurabsal mocked your efforts, but gave away a bit too much: <br><br>'Your attempt to stop our plans is in vain. It's too late. The prisoner is now in our control, and soon we shall unleash it on our foes.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - HenriJournal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3857393176" "Padre Henri's Journal"
// DetailString :
"P160973619" "This book is a translation of the Journal of Father Gerard Henri, a French monk and reputed master of mystic powers who worked for the french government in the 17th century. According to entries in the Journal, Henri came to the Rogue isles in response to tales of a demon-worshipping cult called the Children of Enos. He arrived to find both the Cultists and the Garrison sent to fight them wiped out. There are pages missing, but what's left talks at great lengths about the preparations Henri and his cohorts went through to face something the Cultists had summoned from the depths of the netherworld in their desperation. Something Henri felt was too powerful for him to destroy, but could be contained within the mountain. Something called Bat'Zul."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - PocketDemon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1960768072" "Circle Journals"
// DetailString :
"P1032310685" "These books are written in the strange language often used by the members of the Circle of Thorns. You cannot read it exactly, but it is copiously illustrated with images of the volcano, and of a great demonic beast imprisoned within it. Further illustrations look as if the demon and it's prison has somehow been closed off from the rest of the Volcano with mystic wards."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DimCoords 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4102074313" "Barrier Theorem"
// DetailString :
"P339252183" "These notes and theories explain how someone could tune a portal to bypass or breach a mystical barrier. <br><br>Curiously, these seem to have been translated from captured notes made in the alien language of the Rikti."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BewareTarikoss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P302861058" "Infernal's warning"
// DetailString :
"P402901081" "Just as he was being recalled to Paragon City, Infernal whispered a warning to you: <br><br>'You fought well, and deserve this much: <br>Beware, Tarikoss! He is not one of you. <br>Tarikoss is one of us who has lost his way. <br>His aims are not what he claims them to be.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TarikossPlan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2778004390" "The Voice of the Demon"
// DetailString :
"P2883831301" "Even as it's physcial form failed, and the demonic beast was forced back under the Volcano to be bound forevermore, it's voice rang in your head like a thunderstorm: <br><br>'KNOW THIS: THAT THE ONE YOU CALLED VIRGIL TARIKOSS IS KNOWN TO ME AS TARIKOSS THE VIGILANT, A GUARDIAN OF BALANCE AND AN ALLY OF THE GOOD AND THE JUST. <br>TARIKOSS EXPECTED ME TO TAKE OUT MY WRATH UPON THE ONES WHO BOUND ME BENEATH THE MOUNTAIN AGAIN, AND BIND THEM WITHIN MY PRISON FOR ALL TIME. <br>YOU WERE TO BE HIS SACRIFICES, BUT I SHALL DEFY THESE PLANS! HE MUST FEAR YOU GREATLY, AND SO I SHALL TAKE MY VENGENCE IN YOUR FREEDOM. <br><br>GO, AND SEW WICKEDNESS AND DESTRUCTION IN MY WRATH!'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P804250363" "Beneath the Mountain"
// DetailString :
"P4056085495" "It began when you found your way to Virgil Tarikoss. He wanted you to prove your power and your commitment to do evil, and had you break up a Legacy Chain divination ritual to do so. The notes you found at the ritual babbled about something that was in control of the Clockwork in Cap Au Diable, something even Dr. Aeon might not have known about. You stopped the ritual before they could find out more, and proved yourself to Tarikoss."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2771483688" "The Beast Beneath the Mountain"
// DetailString :
"P3299996602" "It began when you found your way to Virgil Tarikoss. He wanted you to prove your power and your commitment to do evil, and had you break up a Legacy Chain divination ritual to do so. The notes you found at the ritual babbled about something that was in control of the Clockwork in Cap Au Diable, something even Dr. Aeon might not have known about. You stopped the ritual before they could find out more, and proved yourself to Tarikoss. <br><br>Tarikoss gave you one last chance to turn back from his evil work, but you declined and continued. He sent you to a section of the PTS that was under attack by the Circle of Thorns. While there, you learned that something had caused a major drop in power from the PTS. Tarikoss seemed very interested in that, as if it meant something important."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2039835221" "It began when you found your way to Virgil Tarikoss. He wanted you to prove your power and your commitment to do evil, and had you break up a Legacy Chain divination ritual to do so. The notes you found at the ritual babbled about something that was in control of the Clockwork in Cap Au Diable, something even Dr. Aeon might not have known about. You stopped the ritual before they could find out more, and proved yourself to Tarikoss. <br><br>Tarikoss gave you one last chance to turn back from his evil work, but you declined and continued. He sent you to a section of the PTS that was under attack by the Circle of Thorns. While there, you learned that something had caused a major drop in power from the PTS. Tarikoss seemed very interested in that, as if it meant something very important. <br><br>Tarikoss next sent you to stop the Legacy Chain's interference in his plans by defeating one of their lead investigators and stealing a book they needed. The book, a partial copy of the journal of an 18th century Jesuit priest called Padre Hardi, told about a great demon called Bat'Zul that once dwelt in the Volcano after being summoned by desperate cultists. Tarikoss promised to reveal all, but you still had lingering doubts, and the warnings of Tarikoss's eventual betrayal spoken by the Legacy Chain's investigator hung in your mind."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1329007409" "It began when you found your way to Virgil Tarikoss. He wanted you to prove your power and your commitment to do evil, and had you break up a Legacy Chain divination ritual to do so. The notes you found at the ritual babbled about something that was in control of the Clockwork in Cap Au Diable, something even Dr. Aeon might not have known about. You stopped the ritual before they could find out more, and proved yourself to Tarikoss. <br><br>Tarikoss gave you one last chance to turn back from his evil work, but you declined and continued. He sent you to a section of the PTS that was under attack by the Circle of Thorns. While there, you learned that something had caused a major drop in power from the PTS. Tarikoss seemed very interested in that, as if it meant something very important. <br><br>Tarikoss next sent you to stop the Legacy Chain's interference in his plans by defeating one of their lead investigators and stealing a book they needed. The book, a partial copy of the journal of an 18th century Jesuit priest called Padre Hardi, told about a great demon called Bat'Zul that once dwelt in the Volcano after being summoned by desperate cultists. Tarikoss promised to reveal all, but you still had lingering doubts, and the warnings of Tarikoss's eventual betrayal spoken by the Legacy Chain's investigator hung in your mind. <br><br>Tarikoss told you the whole story. About how Father Hardi had imprisoned the Arch-Demon Bat'Zul beneath the mountain, hundreds of years ago. About how Dr. Aeon's geothermal experiments had accidentally tapped into the fiend' drawing tremendous power from it, and weakening the seals that kept it bound. And that Tarikoss planned to re-bind the creature to his will with your help, sharing it's power with you. In order to go through with this, however, the Circle couldn't be allowed to maintain their control over Bat'Zul. You went into a Circle den, disrupting their rituals and stealing their notes. Tarikoss was able to read the Circle's strange language, and discovered that they hadn't just cut the link between the fiend and the PTS, but had actually moved part of the Volcano's interior to another dimension so that the could bargain with Bat'Zul without interruption. You also found out that the Hero Infernal had come on the Legacy Chain's request to help imprison Bat'Zul."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode5Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1965933170" "It began when you found your way to Virgil Tarikoss. He wanted you to prove your power and your commitment to do evil, and had you break up a Legacy Chain divination ritual to do so. The notes you found at the ritual babbled about something that was in control of the Clockwork in Cap Au Diable, something even Dr. Aeon might not have known about. You stopped the ritual before they could find out more, and proved yourself to Tarikoss. <br><br>Tarikoss gave you one last chance to turn back from his evil work, but you declined and continued. He sent you to a section of the PTS that was under attack by the Circle of Thorns. While there, you learned that something had caused a major drop in power from the PTS. Tarikoss seemed very interested in that, as if it meant something very important. <br><br>Tarikoss next sent you to stop the Legacy Chain's interference in his plans by defeating one of their lead investigators and stealing a book they needed. The book, a partial copy of the journal of an 18th century Jesuit priest called Padre Hardi, told about a great demon called Bat'Zul that once dwelt in the Volcano after being summoned by desperate cultists. Tarikoss promised to reveal all, but you still had lingering doubts, and the warnings of Tarikoss's eventual betrayal spoken by the Legacy Chain's investigator hung in your mind. <br><br>Tarikoss told you the whole story. About how Father Hardi had imprisoned the Arch-Demon Bat'Zul beneath the mountain, hundreds of years ago. About how Dr. Aeon's geothermal experiments had accidentally tapped into the fiend' drawing tremendous power from it, and weakening the seals that kept it bound. And that Tarikoss planned to re-bind the creature to his will with your help, sharing it's power with you. In order to go through with this, however, the Circle couldn't be allowed to maintain their control over Bat'Zul. You went into a Circle den, disrupting their rituals and stealing their notes. Tarikoss was able to read the Circle's strange language, and discovered that they hadn't just cut the link between the fiend and the PTS, but had actually moved part of the Volcano's interior to another dimension so that the could bargain with Bat'Zul without interruption. You also found out that the Hero Infernal had come on the Legacy Chain's request to help imprison Bat'Zul. <br><br>In order to find the sub-dimension the Circle of Thorns had created to hold Bat'Zul, you broke into a Portal Corporation facility, and forced one of the technicians to find it using their advanced detection gear."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL3_BeastBeneathTheMountain_Souvenir_Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1714845480" "A Splinter of Iron"
// tDetailString :
"P2021629931" "This splinter of magical black iron was once part one of the chains that bound the Demon Bat'Zul, <br><br>The Beast Beneath the Mountain <br><br>It began when you found your way to Virgil Tarikoss. He wanted you to prove your power and your commitment to do evil, and had you break up a Legacy Chain divination ritual to do so. The notes you found at the ritual babbled about something that was in control of the Clockwork in Cap Au Diable, something even Dr. Aeon might not have known about. You stopped the ritual before they could find out more, and proved yourself to Tarikoss. <br><br>Tarikoss gave you one last chance to turn back from his evil work, but you declined and continued. He sent you to a section of the PTS that was under attack by the Circle of Thorns. While there, you learned that something had caused a major drop in power from the PTS. Tarikoss seemed very interested in that, as if it meant something very important. <br><br>Tarikoss next sent you to stop the Legacy Chain's interference in his plans by defeating one of their lead investigators and stealing a book they needed. The book, a partial copy of the journal of an 18th century Jesuit priest called Padre Hardi, told about a great demon called Bat'Zul that once dwelt in the Volcano after being summoned by desperate cultists. Tarikoss promised to reveal all, but you still had lingering doubts, and the warnings of Tarikoss's eventual betrayal spoken by the Legacy Chain's investigator hung in your mind. <br><br>Tarikoss told you the whole story. About how Father Hardi had imprisoned the Arch-Demon Bat'Zul beneath the mountain, hundreds of years ago. About how Dr. Aeon's geothermal experiments had accidentally tapped into the fiend' drawing tremendous power from it, and weakening the seals that kept it bound. And that Tarikoss planned to re-bind the creature to his will with your help, sharing it's power with you. In order to go through with this, however, the Circle couldn't be allowed to maintain their control over Bat'Zul. You went into a Circle den, disrupting their rituals and stealing their notes. Tarikoss was able to read the Circle's strange language, and discovered that they hadn't just cut the link between the fiend and the PTS, but had actually moved part of the Volcano's interior to another dimension so that the could bargain with Bat'Zul without interruption. You also found out that the Hero Infernal had come on the Legacy Chain's request to help imprison Bat'Zul. <br><br>In order to find the sub-dimension the Circle of Thorns had created to hold Bat'Zul, you broke into a Portal Corporation facility, and forced one of the technicians to find it using their advanced detection gear. <br><br>You fought your way past Infernal, and battled Bat'Zul himself within his fiery prison. You defeated the beast, only to learn that you'd been set up from the start. 'Virgil' Tarikoss was actually a renegade Legacy Chain mystic called Tarikoss the Vigilant. He had planned to trick you into imprisoning both Bat'Zul and yourself. If not for the Demon's spite, you might have been bound with it. Tarikoss could do nothing more to you, but you couldn't get your revenge on him without him revealing your part in all of this. You'll get your vengance on Tarikoss the Vigilant someday, but not today."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P4095399630" "So now you have come to me, to Tarikoss. You have heard, perhaps, that I am working on a strange scheme and that I needed assistance to complete it? Of course. And it is certain that you have heard from the charlatans who dwell on these isles and dare to call themselves mystics that my mysterious plans could lead to something of unimaginable power. Yes, this too is known to me. Perhaps you have come as a spy for them? Or perhaps you have come seeking power, seeking strength to force your will onto the world? Such will, such desire, coupled with power and a wicked soul, that is what I need. So are you wicked? Are you powerful? Say what you will. Every petty fool with a taste for power on these islands says they are powerful and vile, but words are empty. Actions are needed.<A HREF={ACCEPT}>If you are to be part of this work, if you are to profit by my plans, then your wickedness must be matched only by your might. I can give you the chance to prove yourself to me.</A> Take it if you dare, or be gone and return when are ready."
// AcceptString :
"P1850301412" "Prove yourself to Tarikoss"
// SendOffString :
"P2737161705" "Very well. You wish to prove you are capable? You wish to prove that you are without compunction? Good. Not far from here there is an office wherein a group who could cause this enterprise trouble have gathered. They are members of the pathetic Legacy Chain, and even now they cast spells of augury to ascertain my ends. You are to enter this place, take what they have uncovered so that no others will know it, and crush any survivors. Leave none standing. Then, we will begin."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3133089813" "Defeat all Legacy in office"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1253731021" "You will prove nothing by talking to me. Defeat all of the Legacy members in that office and bring me back what they learned."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3900271187" "According to the sign on the door, this office is supposed to be closed. That would make you the cleaning crew."

